// HoughLines calls C++ datamunge::cv::hough_lines.
//
// Standard Hough line transform: every pixel of `img` whose grayscale luma is >= `edge_threshold`
// votes, in a rho-theta accumulator (theta stepped every degree over
// [0, pi), rho stepped every pixel over the image's diagonal range), for every line
// that could pass through it. Returns every accumulator cell with at least `min_votes`,
// non-max-suppressed within a (2*nms_radius+1) rho-theta cell window so a
// single real line doesn't produce a cluster of near-duplicate near-identical results.
// Intended input is an edge map (e.g. image::sobel_edges()'s output), not a raw photo.
//
// It uses the C++ defaults edgeThreshold = 128, minVotes = 50, nmsRadius = 5;
// [HoughLinesWithEdgeThreshold], [HoughLinesWithMinVotes] and [HoughLinesWithNmsRadius] pass more
// arguments.
func HoughLines(img *Image) ([]*HoughLine, error) {
	return rosetta.Result[[]*HoughLine](rosetta.Call(75, img))
}

